WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.440
Sakaki's special strategy uses Action Cards!

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:09.420
I feel like I've seen this before... 
I wonder where it was.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:13.210
An orange? No, it's something else...

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:19.320
Sawatari, Gongenzaka, and Tsukikage 
have taken no damage,

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:26.460
but Tsukikage's attacks have 
Yuya Sakaki down to 2200 life!

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.470
Keep at it, Yuya!

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.120
Show no mercy, Tsukikage.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.190
Crush Yuya Sakaki!

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:35.680
Reiji...

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:39.490
If you do this, my child will...

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.650
If that's enough to defeat him,

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:46.360
then Yuya was never a good 
enough duelist, to begin with.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.310
Mother,

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:51.560
I am very sorry for what I said.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.030
But you can give up on Layra smiling.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:02.640
It is all my fault that he ended up this way.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:09.830
I only saw him as a tool of 
vengeance against Leo Akaba.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:14.810
Because of that, he lost his smile.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.580
I won't let it happen again!

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:19.530
I'll seal Z-ARC myself!

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.850
I was so wrong!

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:32.370
Forgive me, Layra!

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:35.390
My turn is not yet over.

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:37.610
I activate Kagen's Pendulum Effect.

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:39.850
It earns the Pendulum Effect of Jogen,

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:42.580
the other monster in my Pendulum Zone.

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:44.670
The same as Jogen?

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.180
The piercing effect again?

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:49.920
Battle! Getsuga attacks Hippo Token!

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.140
Getsuga has 2000 attack points!

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:57.210
That's 2000 points of piercing damage!

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:00.140
But Yuya has 2200 life points!

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:01.470
He won't finish the job.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.440
Kagen's second effect activates!

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:07.640
Once per turn, when one of 
my Ninja monsters attacks,

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:11.100
that monster's attack points increase by 500!

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:12.340
What?

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:15.550
Oh! If this goes through, 
his life will fall to 0!

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:19.990
Will Yuya be out of the fight already?!

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:26.420
Implementing mass into Solid Vision 
has created Action Duels.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:31.130
In duels where the field, monsters 
and duelists become one,

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:34.240
the people are caught in a frenzy of excitement!

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:12.960
Overflowing Memories

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:16.010
Hippo!

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:19.340
Laughable.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:22.600
A decoy?

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:26.900
I activate my Action Spell Miracle!

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:32.450
The Hippo Token is not destroyed, 
and battle damage is halved.

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:35.150
Interesting... Let me get in on this!

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:40.010
I activate my trap card Abyss Improv!

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:43.310
I add the attack points of one Abyss Actor,

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:47.370
Level 4 or below, to battle damage dealt.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:51.170
What?

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:53.130
Incredible!

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:56.880
Shingo Sawatari is aiding Tsukikage?!

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.880
Wait a minute!

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:02.120
When no spell or trap cards 
are in my graveyard,

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:05.350
and damage is dealt in a battle 
with a defense-position monster,

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:10.750
I can activate Superheavy Samurai Helper's 
effect by sending it to my graveyard.

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:13.020
I activate Superheavy 
Samurai Helper's effect!

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:15.290
During damage calculation,

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:18.500
I can add the defense points of one 
Superheavy Samurai on my field

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:21.470
to those of another defense-position monster!

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:30.410
Now, Gongenzaka is aiding Sakaki!

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:39.020
And Abyss Improv's effect adds 1100.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:43.260
Tsukikage takes 1600 points of damage!

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:46.760
Sorry, Tsukikage...

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:50.730
I was trying to help, but I guess I hurt you.

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:52.230
It matters not.

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:54.990
When the Battle Phase ends,

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:57.570
Getsuga's attack points return to normal.

00:05:57.910 --> 00:06:00.010
I now end my turn.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:04.460
Thanks! You saved me, Gongenzaka!

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:07.510
Don't get the wrong idea. 
I wasn't saving you.

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:11.810
Yuya! I am the one who will defeat you!

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:16.300
Fine. In that case, 
let's start with those two!

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:17.190
Yeah!

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:23.360
Incredible! It seems this has 
turned into a tag-team duel

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:27.370
between Yuya and Gongenzaka 
versus Tsukikage and Sawatari!

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:29.960
Yuya and Gongenzaka are a team!

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:31.520
Wow, it sounds fun!

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:33.570
It gives me shivers!

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:36.570
The fun is only...

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:37.540
...getting started!

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:39.010
My turn!

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:43.040
I set the Pendulum Scale with 
Scale 1 Stargazer Magician

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:47.590
and Scale 8 Timegazer Magician from my hand!

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:03.440
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 2 and 7 simultaneously!

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:06.400
Swing, my soul's pendulum.

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:09.370
Draw an arc of light in the sky!

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:11.240
Pendulum Summon!

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:12.600
Come out!

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:17.200
The rare dragon with two 
different-colored eyes,

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.780
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:25.490
Battle! I attack Curtain Raiser with 
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:28.420
Spiral Strike Burst!

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:36.630
Riding duels?

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:38.370
Why was I on a motorcycle?

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.430
No, that wasn't a motorcycle.

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:44.810
It was a D-Wheel!

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:46.690
That's right...

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:50.520
We Lancers went to the Synchro Dimension.

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:52.190
Not a chance!

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:55.220
I activate Curtain Raiser's monster effect!

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:59.190
When Curtain Raiser is the sole 
monster on my side of the field,

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:03.480
its attack points are doubled 
during damage calculation!

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:16.750
Reducing your ace monster, Odd-Eyes Pendulum 
Dragon, to a mere 300 damage dealt...

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:18.440
Amazing, aren't I?

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:20.960
The super, ultra, hyper-strong duelist—

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:21.850
Shingo Sawatari...

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:25.720
I attack you directly with 
Performapal Hip Hippo!

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:36.180
I end my turn.

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:41.130
But why did I go to the Synchro Dimension?

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:47.810
For what purpose?

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:52.150
Now, the curtain is rising on 
my entertainment theater!

00:08:53.210 --> 00:09:00.300
I'm the man that the genius duelist Reiji 
Akaba trusted to take down Academia.

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:05.320
And I, Shingo Sawatari, will show you 
the ultimate entertainment duel!

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:07.460
We'll see about that.

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:11.090
You aren't the one who will demonstrate 
the ultimate entertainment duel.

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:12.960
I, the son of their progenitor,

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:15.800
Yusyo Sakaki, intend to do the same!

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:19.640
Well, let us see who the 
true entertainment duelist is.

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:20.100
Yeah!

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:23.010
My turn... Draw!

00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:29.840
I set the Pendulum Scale with 
Scale 3 Abyss Actor — Extras

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.280
and Scale 8 Abyss Actor — Funky Comedian!

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:38.560
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 4 and Level 7 simultaneously!

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:40.440
Pendulum Summon!

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:47.030
Appear, Abyss Actor — Superstar!

00:09:47.030 --> 00:09:49.310
And the second debut...

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:51.960
Abyss Actor — Curtain Raiser!

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:57.940
I activate my trap card, 
Dragon's Shadow Performance!

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:02.150
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:08.120
Edo Phoenix?

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:17.400
Smile World, torn in half...

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:20.340
What was that all about?

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:24.920
Hey, what's going on?

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:26.900
If you're gonna entertain, do it!

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:30.380
I... I tribute Hippo Token

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:34.980
to equip Hip Hippo to Odd-Eyes 
Pendulum Dragon!

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:43.660
This is the true three-level, iron dragon!

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:46.160
You just stacked them up.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:47.100
Let's go.

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:51.200
Time to begin the Sawatari Theater's 
dragon-slaying show!

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:52.360
Act one.

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:55.830
I activate Funky Comedian's Pendulum Effect!

00:10:56.470 --> 00:11:00.540
Once per turn, I can add one Abyss 
Actor Pendulum Monster

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:02.910
to my Extra Deck,

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:07.880
and increase one monster's attack points
 by those of the monster I added!

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:13.320
Superstar's monster effect!

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:20.470
Once per turn, I can add one Abyss Script 
spell card from my deck to my hand.

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:24.260
I add Abyss Script — Shadow Spirit.

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:25.860
I activate it!

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:33.640
Battle...

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:37.700
Abyss Actor — Superstar attacks Hip Hippo!

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:43.680
In that instant, Abyss Script — 
Shadow Spirit's effect

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:48.480
sets the attack points of one monster an 
Abyss Actor on my field is fighting

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:51.660
equal to that monster's defense points.

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:01.960
Now, the difference in attack points is 2800.

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:06.740
If this attack goes through, 
Yuya Sakaki is finished!

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:20.650
Great job, Hippo!

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:24.360
I activate Action Spell Encore!

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:27.700
I activate Action Card Evasion 
in my graveyard!

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:30.940
I negate Superstar's attack!

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:34.270
That was close...

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:38.750
I activate Hazy Shuriken's effect,

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:41.240
sending the card I just added 
to my hand to the graveyard,

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:44.940
dealing 300 points of damage to Yuya Sakaki!

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:48.400
Thought I was out of the woods...

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:51.420
This is really cramping my 
entertainment-duel style!

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:57.340
Get fired up! Fired up! Fired up!

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:01.560
It's no use... I can't remember anything.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:05.330
Why am I so fixated on this...

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:07.340
Grapefruit?

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:11.660
I give up! I give up!

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:17.390
Anyway, I'll put this in my storage room,

00:13:17.390 --> 00:13:19.240
and go watch Yuya's duel.

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:22.950
Don't come in without asking!

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:24.280
Wh-What was that voice?

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:35.530
This isn't a storage room!

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:42.470
It isn't over yet...

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:44.170
Act two is just beginning!

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:48.870
I activate Quick-Play Spell Abyss 
Entertainment from my hand!

00:13:49.270 --> 00:13:53.530
I halve the attack points of one Abyss 
Actor on my side of the field,

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:55.350
to allow it to attack once more.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:00.750
That's right.

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:03.950
The Lancers left the Xyz Dimension

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:07.100
and headed for Duel Academia 
in the Fusion Dimension.

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:10.960
At the time, I was searching for someone.

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:13.340
Better pay attention!

00:14:13.340 --> 00:14:14.330
Battle!

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:18.440
Abyss Actor — Superstar 
attacks Hip Hippo again!

00:14:22.610 --> 00:14:25.960
The effect of my trap card, 
Dragon's Shadow Performance,

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:29.380
means that cards on my side of the 
field can't be destroyed this turn!

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:31.350
But you still take the damage.

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:41.730
What's wrong, Yuya?

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:46.990
I now end my turn.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:50.810
In that instant, the attack points 
of Superstar return to normal,

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:54.740
and the effect of Abyss Script 
— Shadow Spirit ends.

00:14:56.680 --> 00:15:01.250
In that instant, the effect of Dragon's 
Entertainment Shadow ends!

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:06.680
Now, we shall proceed to my 
partner Gongenzaka's turn.

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:10.020
My turn.

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:11.420
Draw!

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:15.310
I set the Pendulum Scale with

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:20.040
Scale 1 Superheavy Samurai General Jade and 
Scale 8 Superheavy Samurai General Coral!

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:27.610
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 2 and Level 7 simultaneously.

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:29.340
Pendulum Summon!

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:30.910
Appear!

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:37.320
Superheavy Samurai Preparation!

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:44.390
And I Normal Summon Superheavy 
Samurai Soulhorns from my hand!

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:51.060
I activate Soulhorns' monster effect!

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:55.820
Once per turn, I can equip it to one of 
my Superheavy Samurai monsters.

00:15:57.400 --> 00:16:01.050
This entertainment duel, 
which wasn't at all exciting

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:04.030
before Gongenzaka's turn, is beginning 
to meet our expectations.

00:16:04.030 --> 00:16:05.340
Let me on for a minute!

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:06.510
Hey... What are you doing?

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:08.350
Just let me use the mike!

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:12.600
Gongenzaka has equipped 
Soulhorns to Big Benkei.

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:16.460
What kind of duel will he show us now?

00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:17.320
Yuya!

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:19.020
You won't want to miss—

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:20.020
Yuzu!

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:21.490
Yuzu isn't here!

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:32.700
Yuzu... Yuzu isn't here!

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:36.760
Yuzu!

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:39.980
That's right... She's been 
gone this whole time.

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:42.780
Why didn't we notice it earlier?

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:44.750
Yuzu...

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:46.720
Yuzu...

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:48.620
Yuzu...

00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:55.350
Yuzu...

00:16:56.590 --> 00:17:00.030
Yuzu... Yuzu... Yuzu!

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:04.790
Has he remembered?

00:17:07.690 --> 00:17:11.680
The world is trying to split 
apart into four again!

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:15.550
Z-ARC wants to separate the 
dimensions and repeat it all—

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:17.080
I won't let it happen again!

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:19.160
I'll seal Z-ARC myself!

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:25.620
At that time, Layra deliberately 
expelled Ray's spirit from his body,

00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:30.640
sealing Z-ARC's evil within 
the depths of his soul.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:35.830
Layra... Layra!

00:17:36.190 --> 00:17:38.520
Then, as a result of the dimensional split,

00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:43.360
Layra, who was reborn 
as a baby, lost his smile.

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:45.810
But I have faith.

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:51.020
That this child will show us 
a gentle smile, someday.

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:52.970
Yes.

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:56.750
Because that was why we 
regained our memories.

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:03.690
Yuya, your true trial begins now.

00:18:06.990 --> 00:18:09.030
Oh, no. Yuya's in trouble.

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:12.370
I will end this duel this turn!

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:17.040
I activate Superheavy Samurai 
Preparation's monster effect!

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:19.550
I pay 1000 of my own life

00:18:19.550 --> 00:18:23.280
to reduce the attack points of 
one opponent monster by 1000!

00:18:25.220 --> 00:18:28.190
I choose Superstar!

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:39.500
I activate the effect one more time!

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:48.160
I activate it a third time—

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:54.580
Wh-What the heck?

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:57.050
That's right...

00:18:57.540 --> 00:19:02.190
I traveled the dimensions, 
searching for Yuzu.

00:19:15.060 --> 00:19:19.370
And then, I finally found her.

00:19:19.890 --> 00:19:21.670
Yuzu! It's me! It's Yuya!

00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:23.640
Don't you recognize me?!

00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:25.860
Yuya?

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:28.280
Yeah, it's me!

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:30.030
You're back to your old self?

00:19:30.030 --> 00:19:31.750
I'm so glad, Yuzu!

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:37.220
I activate Big Benkei's monster effect.

00:19:37.220 --> 00:19:40.840
Big Benkei is able to attack 
from defense position.

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:57.010
And the effect of Soulhorns lets the monster 
it's equipped to attack twice,

00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:59.590
when no spell or trap cards 
are in my graveyard!

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:16.090
And... And then, I...

00:20:17.030 --> 00:20:21.810
During the Battle Phase, Odd-Eyes 
Raging Dragon can attack twice.

00:20:21.810 --> 00:20:22.640
I—

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:24.000
Stop it!

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:25.970
Yuzu...

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:29.810
Please don't become a slave to anger anymore!

00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:32.880
So take them back.

00:20:32.880 --> 00:20:36.790
Smile like the real you!

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:42.060
Ruri!

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:49.230
I attack Pendulum Ruler with 
Odd-Eyes Raging Dragon!

00:20:49.230 --> 00:20:51.700
Yuya!

00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:04.840
I activate Superheavy Samurai 
Preparation's monster effect!

00:21:05.190 --> 00:21:10.810
When one of my Superheavy Samurai monsters 
defeats an opponent monster by battle,

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:14.320
I can destroy two cards in my Pendulum Zone

00:21:14.690 --> 00:21:17.080
to attack once more!

00:21:23.520 --> 00:21:25.340
My role here has ended.

00:21:31.270 --> 00:21:32.270
I...

00:21:32.930 --> 00:21:36.780
And I'm going to keep winning...

00:21:36.780 --> 00:21:41.100
Until I destroy everything in the world!

00:21:44.880 --> 00:21:48.120
Astrograph Sorcerer, 
with power over spacetime,

00:21:48.480 --> 00:21:53.070
use your unfathomable power 
to bring our wishes together!

00:21:54.310 --> 00:21:55.390
I...

00:22:01.310 --> 00:22:04.040
I am... Z-ARC!

00:23:49.090 --> 00:23:50.970
I am inside Layra.

00:23:51.460 --> 00:23:53.670
Z-ARC's evil heart.

00:23:53.670 --> 00:23:56.350
That's why Layra's smile is gone.

00:23:56.350 --> 00:23:57.920
But if Layra could smile again,

00:23:58.760 --> 00:24:02.360
wouldn't the evil heart disappear?

00:24:02.360 --> 00:24:04.720
But what should I do?

00:24:04.720 --> 00:24:06.920
If you're going to sit there 
and worry about it,

00:24:06.920 --> 00:24:10.990
then I, the man Gongenzaka, will save Yuzu!

00:24:11.520 --> 00:24:15.210
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Supreme King's Soul.

00:24:15.210 --> 00:24:17.400
The fun is only getting started!
